Test a host name's addresses and test ports at once. resolveHostName() connected to one address
after another with a 3 second timeout each, and LiStartConnection() tried TCP 47984, 47989 and
48010 one after another, so a stale or unreachable address (an AAAA record without an IPv6 path)
cost 3 seconds per address and port before a working one was tried, up to 9 seconds when nothing
answered. probeAddressPorts() now starts a non-blocking connect to every test port of the first 8
addresses together and takes the earliest address in getaddrinfo's order that accepts one of its
ports: once one answers, an earlier address still trying gets 250 ms more. The losing sockets are
closed. resolveHostNameOnPorts() takes the three ports; resolveHostName() keeps its one port and
TCP_PORT_FLAG_ALWAYS_TEST. A single address without that flag is still taken untested, and the IPv4
fallback for a synthesized IPv6 address is unchanged. The Rust engine probes the same way
(net::probe). Applies after decode-queue-bound.patch.

